      "content": "#include \"knn.h\"\n#include <string.h>\n\ntypedef struct {\n    float distance;\n    char label;\n} KNNEntry;\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    KNNEntry * entries = (KNNEntry *) malloc(sizeof(KNNEntry) * k);\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        entries[i].distance = -1.0f;\n        entries[i].label = -1;\n    }\n\n    float px = to_evaluate.x;\n    float py = to_evaluate.y;\n\n    int i, j;\n    for (i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        Group g = groups[i];\n        Point * pts = g.points;\n        int len = g.length;\n        char lbl = g.label;\n        for (j = 0; j < len; j++) {\n            float dx = pts[j].x - px;\n            float dy = pts[j].y - py;\n            float d = dx*dx + dy*dy;\n\n            if (k > 0 && entries[k-1].distance != -1.0f && d >= entries[k-1].distance) {\n                continue;\n            }\n\n            int pos = 0;\n            while (pos < k && entries[pos].distance != -1.0f && entries[pos].distance <= d) {\n                pos++;\n            }\n            if (pos < k) {\n                size_t count = (size_t)(k - pos - 1);\n                if (count > 0) {\n                    memmove(&entries[pos+1], &entries[pos], sizeof(KNNEntry) * count);\n                }\n                entries[pos].distance = d;\n                entries[pos].label = lbl;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    char * labels = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * k);\n    for (i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        labels[i] = entries[i].label;\n    }\n    qsort(labels, k, sizeof(char), compare_for_sort);\n\n    char most_frequent = labels[0];\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\n    int current_frequency = 1;\n\n    for (i = 1; i < k; i++) {\n        if (labels[i] != labels[i - 1]) {\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n            }\n\n            current_frequency = 1;\n        } else {\n            current_frequency++;\n        }\n\n        if (i == k - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n            most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n        }\n    }\n\n    free(entries);\n    free(labels);\n\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n    \n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}\n",
      "path": "src/knn.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Packing distance/label pairs into a contiguous struct array improves cache locality during insertion shifts; skipping points whose squared distance is at least the current worst kept distance avoids O(k) scans for most points; using memmove replaces the manual shift loop with an optimized block copy. These changes reduce memory traffic and should speed up the KNN search.",
  "notes": "Only src/knn.c was modified. The header, parsing logic, output format, and tie-breaking behavior (via qsort on labels) are preserved exactly. The new code hoists query coordinates out of loops, uses a packed struct for distance/label pairs to improve locality during shifts, skips points that cannot enter the k-nearest set, and replaces the manual element-by-element shift with memmove.",
